1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind and a sound body.

2
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:16,140
The battle against arachnophobia and the Kishin continues.

3
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,440
There's no hope for you now.

4
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:22,420
Blackstar settled his score with Mifune.

5
00:00:22,420 --> 00:00:33,660
Dad was able to join the battle by using Broom to turn all of Death's city into a robot.

6
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:47,380
What now?

7
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:51,420
And finally...

8
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:54,060
We recaptured the Kishin.

9
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:24,060
We recaptured the Kishin.

10
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:25,060
We recaptured the Kishin.

11
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:26,700
We recaptured the Kishin.

12
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:28,340
We recaptured the Kishin.

13
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:29,340
We recaptured the Kishin.

14
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:34,980
We recaptured the Kishin.

15
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:53,020
He

16
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:59,900
I've kissed black dunhual pink

17
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:02,760
If I picture like you're blind

18
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:07,340
When you will see you

19
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:09,160
You'll see for forever with your soul

20
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:12,540
I will see as Zoho

21
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:18,040
You'll see the light light

22
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:48,520
I have to say, you're as reckless now as you always were.

23
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:53,520
It's nice to see you again too, Ashura.

24
00:02:53,520 --> 00:03:00,520
This is one pleasure I would have been more than happy to forego.

25
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:07,520
The tension is palpable. Even here I feel too close to the Kishan's madness for comfort.

26
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:12,520
The Grim Reaper at his finest, wielding a Death Scythe.

27
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:16,520
And Ashura, the Kishan who has already escaped once.

28
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:19,520
Which one will win this fight?

29
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:24,520
I'm sorry for the inconvenience, but there's no running away this time.

30
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:29,520
You can't leave this room without my permission, which I don't intend to give you.

31
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:34,520
You put me in a difficult position. If you won't let me leave, I'll have to kill you.

32
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:41,520
Oh? Is that so? After all this time, you actually believe you can defeat me?

33
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:53,520
Unfortunately for you, the moment you were swallowed and trapped in my death room, the winner was already decided.

34
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:59,520
Well, what do you say? Shall we end this quickly?

35
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:03,520
It's starting. The battle between gods.

36
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:13,520
Lord Death wields a Death Scythe. Just one step from utter darkness?

37
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:28,520
Hey, Maka. What the hell's going on out there? Why's Death Scythe moving? What happened to the Kishan?

38
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:34,520
Without even using my soul perception, I can tell. The Kishan is inside the Death Room right now.

39
00:04:34,520 --> 00:04:35,520
Seriously?

40
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:38,520
He's not alone. Lord Death's in there too.

41
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:39,520
So now what?

42
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:41,520
Let's keep moving.

43
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:42,520
Let's keep moving.

44
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,520
Are we going to the Death Room?

45
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:55,520
The Kishan isn't the only target. There's still Arachne and the moral manipulation machine. Let's just do what we can out here for now. First we have to meet up with the others. Sound good?

46
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:57,520
Yeah. Let's do it.

47
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:11,520
Which way now?

48
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,520
From here we go left.

49
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,520
Left? Okay. Which way is left?

50
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:20,520
Just take a deep breath, Black Star. Left is the side you hold a fork on.

51
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:23,520
Kick!

52
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:28,520
No! Come back here, Black Star! Wrong way! That's the side you hold a knife on!

53
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,520
I know that!

54
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:37,520
Yes, naturally. Of course you knew Black Star.

55
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:40,520
Didn't look like he knew to me.

56
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:56,520
This is crazy! What's going on up there?

57
00:05:56,520 --> 00:06:00,520
I don't understand this. Neither one of them has even made a move yet.

58
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:03,520
Look closely. The fight's begun.

59
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,520
Little Super Saiyan.

60
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:09,520
Little Super Saiyan.

61
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:24,520
Big Star.

62
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:25,520
Big Star.

63
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,520
Nice try. But it looks like the next move is mine.

64
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,520
Big Star- What do you say, Spirit? You ready?

65
00:06:28,520 --> 00:06:29,520
Big Star- Whatever you are...

66
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,520
What do you say, spirit? You ready?

67
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:33,520
Whatever you are.

68
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:37,520
Then let's end this traitor! He's lived long enough!

69
00:06:49,520 --> 00:06:51,520
He did it!

70
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:53,520
Fools!

71
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:55,520
This doesn't look right. It's a decoy!

72
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:57,520
Damn it!

73
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:01,520
Damn it!

74
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,520
Come on, Dad!

75
00:07:21,520 --> 00:07:25,520
Is that the best you can manage?

76
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:31,520
Maybe you should have rested up a bit more before taking me on!

77
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:36,520
Can you do me a favor? Stop talking in that dumb voice. It's incredibly annoying.

78
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:44,520
If it bothers you so much, let me kill you quickly! Don't worry, I'll make it painless!

79
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:48,520
Why don't we have a little chat about the past instead?

80
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:54,520
You see, I've had an awful lot to think about ever since you locked me up.

81
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:56,520
There was no escaping it.

82
00:07:56,520 --> 00:08:00,520
When you're sealed inside a bag of your own skin, there's only so much you can do.

83
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:02,520
Your mind starts to wander.

84
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,520
Yeah, sorry about that!

85
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:06,520
It won't happen again!

86
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,520
This time, you'll be good and dead!

87
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:14,520
I know he's the Lord of Death, but I've never heard him sound so murderous before!

88
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:23,520
Sitting there in the dark, I had the chance to think about a lot of things, including the nature of the world itself.

89
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:27,520
And after lengthy consideration, I realized something.

90
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:31,520
When all is said and done, this world is an unknowable place.

91
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:36,520
On the surface, all appears rational, orderly.

92
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:39,520
But what lies beyond that thin veneer of reason?

93
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,520
Stability and reality?

94
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:43,520
Or chaos and madness?

95
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,520
What are we really made of in the end?

96
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:49,520
Is there truly any meaning to the lives we lead?

97
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:52,520
Or are we nothing more than hollow vessels?

98
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:55,520
These are questions we can never answer.

99
00:08:55,520 --> 00:09:00,520
Because we cannot hope to see beyond the world's fragile layer of skin.

100
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:05,520
So we live our lives filled with uncertainty.

101
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:09,520
Never knowing who or what we truly are or what the future will bring.

102
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:12,520
All we can do is imagine.

103
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:17,520
Life becomes an unsolvable mystery with any number of twists and turns awaiting us.

104
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:21,520
And that's enough to fill any soul with terror.

105
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:24,520
So much time to think, and that's all you could come up with?

106
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,520
You're really pathetic!

107
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:29,520
REVERSE!

108
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:45,520
It's not necessarily the uncertainty that makes us fearful.

109
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,520
It's more than that.

110
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:51,520
The answers we imagine are what really frighten us.

111
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:52,520
Let me get this straight.

112
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:57,520
You're saying people would be happier if they stopped imagining altogether?

113
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:00,520
Imagination is where all our fear originates.

114
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:04,520
It is the mother of terror and mankind's greatest weakness.

115
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:09,520
I always thought it was humans' greatest strength, what separates them from the animals.

116
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:15,520
What you offer is order and authority, which gives humans the illusion of security and peace.

117
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:21,520
But what truly lies under the thin layer of rationality you attempt to impose on the world?

118
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:23,520
Who knows?

119
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:24,520
Who knows?

120
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:25,520
Exactly.

121
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:28,520
Maybe there's nothing under there at all.

122
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:32,520
I think I've just about had it with listening to this meaningless chatter.

123
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:34,520
Ready, spirit?

124
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:35,520
Yeah, let's do it.

125
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,520
Yeah, let's do it.

126
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,520
Let's go!

127
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:41,520
Slow resonance!

128
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,520
Ashura!

129
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:47,520
Your time is up!

130
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:51,520
Is it?

131
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:52,520
She said, Hunter!

132
00:10:52,520 --> 00:11:18,520
You've lost an arm.

133
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:22,520
I'm not too worried about it.

134
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:24,520
It'll grow back quickly enough.

135
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:35,520
This fight of theirs is like nothing I've seen.

136
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:38,520
You think I wasn't expecting that?

137
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,520
I know who I'm dealing with here.

138
00:11:41,520 --> 00:11:43,520
Pain in the present can be dealt with.

139
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:47,520
It's imagining future pain that hurts us the most.

140
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,520
It terrifies us.

141
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,520
So what?

142
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:54,520
Pain and death are not so frightening, really.

143
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:57,520
Unless you let your imagination run away with you.

144
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:59,520
Again, so what?

145
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:02,520
Is there a point in all this babbling of yours?

146
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:03,520
Naturally.

147
00:12:04,520 --> 00:12:06,520
Would you like to hear it?

148
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:08,520
Very well, then.

149
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:09,520
It's quite simple.

150
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:11,520
Sea Reaper,

151
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:14,520
I have decided not to imagine anymore.

152
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:18,520
What?

153
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:19,520
What?

154
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:20,520
Subaki?

155
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:21,520
Do you think we can move a bit more quietly?

156
00:12:21,520 --> 00:12:22,520
Why should we?

157
00:12:22,520 --> 00:12:23,520
Turning left and right is making things difficult.

158
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:27,520
It's much easier to do things my way and go straight forward.

159
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:28,520
Yes, okay.

160
00:12:28,520 --> 00:12:30,520
But if we make too much noise, the enemy will find us.

161
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:31,520
Let them come!

162
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:32,520
I'll take them down one by one!

163
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:33,520
Is this what he's always like?

164
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:34,520
Is this what he's always like?

165
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:35,520
Well, yeah, more or less.

166
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:36,520
What's Blackstar for you?

167
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,520
He's an incredibly straightforward kind of person.

168
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:38,520
It's you!

169
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,520
Yeah, it is me!

170
00:12:39,520 --> 00:12:40,520
I'm trying to be a bit weird!

171
00:12:40,520 --> 00:12:41,520
Oh, I'm trying to make it easier to do things my way and go straight forward.

172
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:42,520
Yes, okay.

173
00:12:42,520 --> 00:12:44,520
But if we make too much noise, the enemy will find us.

174
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:45,520
Let them come!

175
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:47,520
I'll take him down one by one!

176
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:52,520
Is this what he's always like?

177
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:53,520
Well, yeah, more or less.

178
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:54,520
What's Blackstar for you?

179
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:57,520
He's an incredibly straightforward kind of person.

180
00:12:57,520 --> 00:12:59,520
I'm an incredibly straightforward kind of person.

181
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:06,520
It's you!

182
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:09,520
Yeah, it is me! The one and only Black Star!

183
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:13,520
Got you right in the balls!

184
00:13:13,520 --> 00:13:15,520
One point for me!

185
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:17,520
Is that what she's always like?

186
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:19,520
Sorry about that.

187
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:21,520
She's a pretty straightforward person too.

188
00:13:27,520 --> 00:13:31,520
I can't do anything about the barrier the Reaper set up.

189
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,520
My castle is in ruins.

190
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:37,520
Must I now merely sit here and quietly watch?

191
00:13:37,520 --> 00:13:39,520
Lady Arachne,

192
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:41,520
the situation is serious.

193
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,520
You should escape while you can.

194
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:45,520
I will not.

195
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,520
I'm not going anywhere just yet.

196
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:49,520
But...my lady...

197
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:51,520
I'll wait for him.

198
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:53,520
Ashura will return to my embrace once again.

199
00:13:53,520 --> 00:13:55,520
I'm certain.

200
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:59,520
That's what I have to believe.

201
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:03,520
So, you've decided to sacrifice your imagination.

202
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:05,520
Sounds like a cowardly move.

203
00:14:05,520 --> 00:14:07,520
Cowardly Reaper?

204
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:10,520
I think you should choose your words more carefully.

205
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:13,520
If there's a better word to describe you,

206
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,520
I don't know what it might be!

207
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:21,520
This is how you've been as long as I've known you.

208
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:23,520
Hiding cowardice behind cutting.

209
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:29,520
You were always riddled with insecurities and plagued by fears.

210
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:33,520
Unable to relax until you'd hidden them all.

211
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:35,520
In an effort to escape your own petty fear,

212
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:37,520
you partnered with Vajra.

213
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:39,520
You should have fought alongside me,

214
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:41,520
but you were too weak for that.

215
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:49,520
In the end, you betrayed not only innocent humans,

216
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:53,520
but your own weapon partner as well.

217
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:57,520
You know, for a Grim Reaper, you're impressively naive.

218
00:14:57,520 --> 00:15:01,520
Following the rules doesn't guarantee an escape from fear.

219
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,520
And insanity does.

220
00:15:03,520 --> 00:15:05,520
Even if you bury your fears in madness,

221
00:15:05,520 --> 00:15:07,520
new fears will only surface.

222
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:11,520
Are you truly so lost already that you can't understand that simple fact?

223
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:13,520
If you continue along the path you've chosen,

224
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:15,520
the world will sink into despair.

225
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:19,520
Even a child would see the heartless evil in that.

226
00:15:19,520 --> 00:15:31,520
Don't you see how empty and meaningless the authority you impose is?

227
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,520
That's not how the truth is found.

228
00:15:33,520 --> 00:15:39,520
You make your followers feel safe by offering them white lies and comforting words.

229
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:43,520
Don't you know that only harms them more?

230
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:47,520
There's no hope for you.

231
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,520
You are beyond saving.

232
00:15:49,520 --> 00:15:54,520
Do you find creating the illusion of peace for people that noble of a job?

233
00:15:55,520 --> 00:16:01,520
It's far more noble than seeking to destroy them with blind insanity like you intend to.

234
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:05,520
Have you been listening to a word I've said, old man?

235
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:10,520
What's wrong with surrendering to madness?

236
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,520
That's where the true peace is.

237
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:14,520
So you keep saying.

238
00:16:14,520 --> 00:16:17,520
But that's because you're not strong enough for sanity.

239
00:16:17,520 --> 00:16:19,520
I'm plenty strong.

240
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,520
You'll find out soon enough that you're the weak one, Reaper.

241
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:27,520
What's happening now, kid?

242
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:32,520
Hey, maybe it's time to get out of here.

243
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:37,520
They're fighting with so much power.

244
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:40,520
I was hoping I'd be able to help Dad out.

245
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,520
But that's impossible.

246
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:46,520
I'm a Death Scythe, but this is beyond even my level.

247
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:50,520
Still, it's taking all my willpower not to get involved.

248
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:54,520
It's about time for us to end this.

249
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:58,520
Exactly what I was thinking.

250
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:00,520
Perhaps you should say goodbye to your son.

251
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:05,520
What? Is it something I said?

252
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:09,520
I'll remove your threat once and for all.

253
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:13,520
I'm the guardian of this world.

254
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:16,520
It is my job to make sure you do no further damage to it.

255
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:18,520
So I hear.

256
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:20,520
That's most unfortunate, though.

257
00:17:20,520 --> 00:17:23,520
I'd hoped we'd be able to come to an understanding.

258
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:24,520
No.

259
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:27,520
That was never even a possibility.

260
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:29,520
We were friends once.

261
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:32,520
So allow me to offer you one small piece of advice.

262
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:35,520
You should be careful about hiding behind authority

263
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:38,520
and blinding yourself to the realities of the world.

264
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:40,520
Might cost you your life someday.

265
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:43,520
Or somebody else's.

266
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:11,520
Who can I love?

267
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:19,520
Where's Dad?

268
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:21,520
Father?

269
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:26,520
Where are you?

270
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,520
Dad, no!

271
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:38,280
This is the destruction the whole world will know.

272
00:18:40,060 --> 00:18:42,720
It seems you've learned a lot over the years.

273
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:44,280
But tell me something, Ashura.

274
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:48,900
After you've filled the world to the brim with your insanity,

275
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:50,680
what else will remain?

276
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:52,700
Oh, it's you, Excalibur.

277
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:54,880
Don't worry.

278
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:56,960
Madness is enough.

279
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:59,840
The world doesn't need anything else.

280
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:01,020
Fool!

281
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:03,120
Aw, I've missed you, too.

282
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:05,100
But you're wrong.

283
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:07,200
I've won.

284
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:10,640
It was always going to end this way.

285
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:14,100
Bound as he was by honor and obligation,

286
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:17,220
it was almost too easy to lead him into my trap.

287
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:17,860
Fool!

288
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:22,180
Those in power have the responsibility to maintain honor.

289
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:24,620
Exactly my point.

290
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,500
That's why the Reaper lost.

291
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:30,540
He was too weak, a slave to his own honor.

292
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,340
He lost to me because of his love for other people.

293
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:50,560
No, this is wrong.

294
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:52,680
Very, very wrong.

295
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:55,300
I have to deal with this immediately.

296
00:19:55,860 --> 00:19:57,380
If it continues, I...

297
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:59,260
I can't waste time!

298
00:20:00,220 --> 00:20:01,020
Where'd he go?

299
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:07,000
It's Ashura.

300
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:08,940
He beat Lord Death?

301
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:10,680
That's impossible.

302
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:25,060
Oh, Ashura.

303
00:20:25,060 --> 00:20:25,140
Oh, Ashura.

304
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:35,320
I always trusted you.

305
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:37,160
I knew you'd return.

306
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:39,820
I knew you'd be by my side again.

307
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:43,440
I've been so worried about you this whole time.

308
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:45,760
You have?

309
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:47,060
Yes.

310
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:50,700
Arachne.

311
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:53,200
Yes, love.

312
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:55,560
It's just that I'm afraid.

313
00:20:56,560 --> 00:20:57,800
It's all right, dear.

314
00:20:58,480 --> 00:20:59,600
I'll protect you.

315
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,500
No, Yusi.

316
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:03,620
I'm scared of you.

317
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:23,560
A witch's soul.

318
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:23,580
A witch's soul.

319
00:21:23,580 --> 00:21:42,340
A witch's soul.

320
00:21:42,340 --> 00:22:12,320
Thank you.

321
00:22:12,340 --> 00:22:42,320
Thank you.

322
00:22:42,340 --> 00:23:12,320
Thank you.

323
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:13,600
Have you showered?

324
00:23:13,900 --> 00:23:14,200
Yeah.

325
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:15,480
Brushed your teeth?

326
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:15,960
Yeah.

327
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:17,260
Washed your face?

328
00:23:17,380 --> 00:23:17,600
Yeah.

329
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:18,880
Eaten breakfast?

330
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:19,420
Yeah.

331
00:23:19,940 --> 00:23:20,900
Gotten dressed?

332
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:21,400
Yeah.

333
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:22,980
Clipped your toenails?

334
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,920
Uh, why would I do that?

335
00:23:25,500 --> 00:23:27,760
Well, I guess you're not ready then, are you?

336
00:23:28,020 --> 00:23:30,740
On the next episode of Soul Eater, Ashura wakes.

337
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:32,080
To the end of the world?

338
00:23:32,460 --> 00:23:34,460
Watch it, or I'll take your soul.

